# SDLC Agêntico Version
version: "3.3.0"
build_date: "2026-04-15"
release_notes: |
  v3.3.0 — SDD, BMAD and Harness Engineering activated natively.

  HIGHLIGHTS
  - Constitution v1.0.0 ratified (.specify/memory/constitution.md) with
    11 principles enforced across agents, gates and hooks.
  - Native Spec-Driven Development commands:
    /constitution, /specify, /plan, /tasks, /clarify, /analyze.
  - BMAD planning/dev bifurcation: /bmad-plan, /bmad-dev + deterministic
    complexity detector at .claude/skills/bmad-integration/scripts/detect_level.py.
  - Copilot Cloud Agent is now the default parallelization strategy for
    Phase 6 (ADR-002). parallel-workers kept as fallback for local-env tasks.
    New skill: .claude/skills/copilot-cloud-agent with dispatcher,
    status-tracker and review-relay (bandit + ruff + in-process secret scan).
  - Agent contracts mandatory: 6 tier-1 strict + 34 tier-2 — 40/40 agents covered.
  - Resilience layer: retry / timeout / circuit-breaker primitives at
    .claude/lib/python/resilience.py.
  - Eval harness: 9 regression suites, 79 golden cases covering gate-evaluator,
    code-reviewer, threat-modeler, bmad-detect-level, resilience, settings-lint,
    agent-contracts, parallelization-routing, runbooks.
  - SLOs formalized in .claude/config/slos.yml with burn-rate Grafana dashboard
    and 4 runbooks (6 more explicitly pending).

  ARCHITECTURAL DECISIONS
  - ADR-001: all hooks must resolve paths via $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR.
  - ADR-002: Copilot Cloud Agent as default Phase 6 parallel strategy.

  BREAKING
  - phase-2-to-3 gate is now a blocking gate. It refuses advancement
    unless .specify/specs/<slug>/spec.md has status=approved, constitution_version
    frontmatter, Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and clarify_rounds_completed >= 1.
  - Hook commands in .claude/settings.json must use ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-.}
    prefix; relative paths break sessions when cwd drifts.

  DEFERRED (on purpose, see issue #149)
  - refactoring-surgeon agent (named-smell -> named-refactoring catalog).
